-- dimensions are encoded as a cube built by recursion on their number, so at a variable number
-- every operation is a stuck recursion. Answered 2026-11-13 (the question is the standard
-- semantics, not one for Avik): in CCHM a term in Γ; Ψ; φ means a family natural in the stage, an
-- element of A at every Ψ′ with a substitution f : Ψ′ → Ψ satisfying φ, commuting with every
-- further substitution; a dimension's value at a stage is an element of the free De Morgan algebra
-- on that stage's names, and the substitutions are maps of that algebra (the cubical-set model). So
-- the number of dimensions is variable only in the meta-level quantification over stages, and a
-- semantic action of interval expressions defined on syntax must be shown to respect the algebra's
-- equations once: that is the well-definedness of the cube category's action, not an artefact of
