-- The construction (2026-11-15, derived with Avik; this note supersedes every plan for this goal
-- written before it). Scope, from §6.1's own text: the object language is Π, Σ, PathP and a base type
-- (Bool); the paper fixes reify and reflect at Π, Σ and PathP, normalize = reify ∘ eval ∘
-- reflectContext, the fundamental lemma by induction on typed syntax, and (6.5) eval(reify v, ρ) =
-- denote(v, ρ). Composition, Glue and universes are interpreted by the model's own Kan operations and
-- are not normalized: §6.1 says its clauses describe that fragment. Normalizing them is not this goal.
-- Why dimensions are cube directions (forced in CCHM): reifying a path is pathLam(i. reify(pathApp(p,
-- i))), whose code mentions i as a variable of the code. If an object dimension were a host interval,
-- reification pointwise would be a host family of codes indexed by the interval, and every path in
-- the data type Code is constant, so the code could not depend on i. And an environment cannot hold a
-- host interval (I is not a type). So an object dimension is a name in the context, read as a
-- direction of the cube the meanings live over: a context with n dimensions means an n-fold cube of
-- environments, a term a cube over it (the cubical-set model, stages as host cubes).
-- What that forces, and nothing more:
