-- The checker (derived 2026-11-15). Bidirectional over Der as it stands: check mode for λ, pair, path
-- λ, true and false against a type's meaning; inference for variables, application, projections,
-- case and path application; types inferred. Case carries its motive in its code (done: without it,
-- checking a case needs a motive P with P x the given type, higher-order unification, and one code
-- has derivations at motives agreeing at true and false but not at x). Der's binder premises live
-- in contexts built from the conclusion's meaning (ext-h at the family, lam-ctx at the λ), so each
-- binder case builds the conclusion's meaning from the premise's by abstraction over the extended
-- cube, and carries the premise's derivation across the path of contexts that dcube-map fusion gives
-- (comp over Der, as der-tr; done: abs-mean, der-ext). One1 is the singleton of Bool in Type (done), so
-- Bool types are equal by contraction. Conversion is needed where an inferred term is checked and,
-- for every path λ checked against a PathP, between its body's faces and the type's endpoints, even
-- on normal forms. Sound conversion of term meanings is completeness of normalization: from equal
-- normal codes conclude equal meanings. (6.5) holds by refl because a typed code carries its
-- meaning, so this converse is a theorem of its own: neither a checker run on normal forms nor
-- reification gives it, since a computability witness is not unique for a meaning until it is
-- proved. It is a Kripke relation between two meanings, proved by induction on Der like fund
-- (Abel, Coquand and Dybjer's PER model for decidability of conversion).
-- What elab needs besides (derived 2026-11-15): (a) values typed by a type known only up to a path
-- (an argument against a domain, a pair's components, case's branches against the motive at true
-- and false, a PathP's endpoints against its line's faces) are transported pointwise, by a cube of
-- paths over the base mapped by the pair of cubes (so each vertex's path starts at that vertex's
-- value judgmentally), then dcube-pull; (b) check mode takes the expected type with its derivation
-- (a pair's codomain premise and a λ's domain premise need codes), and inference returns the type's
-- derivation with the term's: a variable's from TCtx, weakened; an application's result type by
-- reading the Π type's codomain off its computability (fund, then rr at the codomain), with no
-- inversion of Der; (c) path application parses its interval code to a canonical form and checks
-- dnf-code of it equal to the code (code-dec), canonical and non-constant (dnf-canon, dnf-nonconst),
-- 0 and 1 by dpapp0 and dpapp1. Checker status (2026-11-15): elab-n checks types Bool, Π, Σ; variables,
-- application, projections, true/false, λ, pairs, case, and the switch from inference (tested); open:
-- conversion at PathP shapes, by determinacy (everything else done; conversion at shapes without
-- PathP is a contraction, their semantic types being contractible; check-code is the checker). Done so far: code-dec, abs-mean/der-ext, dcube-contr/mean1-path,
-- retype (a meaning paired with a term's values carried pointwise along a path of types, with its two
-- projections). Next (derived): elab works over a checking context, Γ with the identity's computable
-- environment and each variable's type's computability (extended under ext-h at any Y, h, M by
-- var-comp, which is general, and comp-ren-e along world-wk; under dext by world-dwk); check mode
-- carries the expected type's computability (rty reifies a λ's domain code and rty-fam-cod a pair's
-- codomain code from it, the body's expected type is the Π clause at world-wk and the new variable);
-- inference returns the type's computability with the term (a variable's from the context, an
-- application's result from the Π clause at the identity world, projections from Σ's, path
-- application from PathP's first component).
-- The completeness this needs, stated (derived 2026-11-15): reify of a meaning reads a code off a
-- computability witness, and its NN is indexed by the meaning itself; so equal normal codes give equal
-- meanings exactly when NN is determinate: two NN derivations of one code over one context, at one
-- type (for normal forms) or at any type (for neutrals, whose shape and type then also agree), have
-- equal meanings. Under binders the contexts are built from the conclusions' meanings (lam-ctx at X,
-- ext-h at R), equal only along the path the induction produces, so the statement carries a path of
-- contexts and concludes a path of meanings over it; a neutral's shape comes from its head's type, so
-- it carries a path of shapes too. It is proved by induction on the first derivation with the second
-- matched against it, mismatched constructors refuted by the code path (no confusion of Code's
-- constructors). This determinacy is the whole content of conversion's soundness; with it, conv is
-- normalize both, code-dec, then the two NN's meanings equal. Without it no checker can accept a
-- path λ against a PathP (its faces against the endpoints) or an inferred term against a non-Bool
-- type.
-- Minimality is correctness (Avik, 2026-11-15): hyperactivity asserts minimality, so code that repeats
-- one reasoning per case is incorrect, not merely large, and work built on it has negative value
-- until it is factored. lib/nbe.cub violates it in five places: the checker's per-rule assembly; NN
-- and Der as two parallel families (ren-nn/ren-der, nn-tr/der-tr, nn-fm-in/der-fm-in); term/type lemma
-- pairs (comp-tr/ty-tr, comp-fm/ty-fm, comp-tm/comp-ty) that JZ/JC already abstract; Π and Σ
-- duplicated at the type level (Fam, CompE's type clause, rty, dty); and the cube layer re-proving
-- path application's naturality per property (papp-lit/conj/dnf × ren, nat, pull, lift, deg, of) and
-- one fusion lemma per pair of structural cube maps. The factored form: one generic cube map (a map
-- over a total base) with one fusion law, path application's naturality stated once; one derivation
-- family indexed by a normal/neutral/any tag with one constructor over a rule table (a rule: its data
-- type, its code constructor, its premises as kind, shape, projection of the data and context
-- transform, its semantic clause), so fund, renaming, rr, determinacy and the checker are each one
-- generic case. This precedes everything else in this node.
-- The cube layer, factored (2026-11-16): lib/cube.cub writes each line operation once over a path of
-- types (LnF), path application as one fold over interval expressions with its displayed fold (pfold,
-- dfold), the diagonal at a name and a cube map's action as folds over the skeleton (gdiag/dgdiag,
-- skfold/dskfold), and one commutation lemma per fold for maps over a fixed base, one for maps that move
-- the base, the fold on a section, and the total map (pfold-tot); every per-form lemma of the old file
-- (papp-lit/conj-from/conj/dnf-from × deg, nat, dmap, of, pull, lift, cmap, fmap; M0, M1, g1) is an
-- instance. Two forms remain both, as distinct statements: a path over refl is not a homogeneous path
-- (the host has no regularity), so fixed-base and base-moving commutation are separate lemmas. Still
-- open in lib/nbe-model.cub: the skeleton-recursive families copied from the old file (skip/keep, cmap-*-d,
-- dexd, ddv, pex, law, sc-, kl-) as instances of gdiag-nat/skfold-nat, and the other four places above.
